/* ── Segmented control, list toolbar, key line [kpadopt-controls] ── */
@layer kp.signature {

/* ── The dashboard parts: action tiles, status rows, the facet list, the heat grid, the matrix, the bar in a cell, the
   week agenda and the run timeline [kpadopt2] ──
   Brutalism's own (themes/brutalism/CHARACTER.md): a tile is the slab, white in the 3 px ink line on its 6 px hard
   shadow, square (G6, G7); pointed at it is inverted, ink ground and yellow words, and nothing moves (the tiles' own
   hover pick); a press drives it onto its footprint, the shadow gone (G14); a failure is taped off, hazard stripes along
   its foot (G13); waiting is the lintel hoisted in its well (G10): a heat grid's row of cells is ONE well with one beam,
   not a well in every cell; the voice is Archivo Black shouting, Space Grotesk in bold capitals (G15). */
@layer kp.signature {

/* ── The dashboard parts: what the package leaves to a register [kpadopt2-repairs] ──
   Formal keeps these parts exactly as Kenny approved them; this theme takes the three repairs the review asks for: a
   loading heat grid or matrix row as tall as its ready row (no skeleton gap between cells), an empty or failed run
   timeline with a lane-sized space for its sentence (never over the legend), the sentence as wide as its words on the
   theme's ground (never through a rule or a ghost bar), and an axis label near the end edge standing before its rule. */
@layer kp.signature {

/* ── The six opt-in options of the dashboard adoption, round 3, in this theme [kpadopt3] ──
   The nav bar's separator, the timeline's day buttons and series runs, the week agenda's upcoming list on a phone and
   the facet swatch's identity pattern (the choice-filter value and the heat grid's End are behaviour only).
   Brutalism's own (themes/brutalism/CHARACTER.md): the separator is a slab of ink as tall as a link;
   lying down across the phone's list it is the divider's hazard band, the yellow hatch on the ink between two ink
   rules. A day on the axis is kicked: pointing lifts it up-left off its hard shadow inside an ink frame, pressed it is
   driven in, the yellow block in the ink frame (as the current page). The upcoming list's day rule is a 2 px ink line;
   the facet pattern is boxed in ink on a hard shadow. */
@layer kp.signature {

/* ── The kpadopt4 data pieces, in this theme [kpadopt4] ──
   Brutalism's own (themes/brutalism/CHARACTER.md): a mark is paint under black ink in the ink line on its small hard
   shadow, square (G5, G6, G7); a part under the hand is lifted up-left off its footprint while its shadow stays on the
   ground (G8); a warning is taped off, hazard stripes along its foot (G13); a number that changes is slammed onto its
   yellow offset (G9); a bolt is square and has its own small shadow (G16); the voice is Archivo Black shouting and Space
   Grotesk speaking in bold capitals, the machine's words in mono (G15). */
@layer kp.signature {

/* ── The uptime strip, rows, checks, choices, a card's four states and the drawings, in this theme [kpadopt4-rows] ──
   A cell of the strip is a small block of paint in its ink line (up, degraded and down are the statuses' paint and the
   stripes they already carry); pointing lifts it up-left off its footprint (G8). A row says its state in a bar of paint
   along its start edge, a failed one taped off, the next one up the yellow slab (G5, G13). A tile of choices is a
   slab: pointing lifts it, the pick is yellow (G5, G8). Waiting is the lintel hoisted in its well (G10): the strip
   is one well, not a well in every cell. The drawings are set down one after another and stop dead (G1, G3). */
@layer kp.signature {

/* ── Flows and records, in this theme [kpadopt4-flows] ──
   A secret printed on the page is slammed onto its yellow offset when it is shown, and its time runs out in ten hard
   steps of a six-pixel bar (G9, G11, G16); a dialog's sections are ruled off in the ink line, the danger section taped
   off (G13); a moment on the timeline is a square bolt with its own small shadow, a stretch in warning is hazard tape
   (G16); a journey is a path of blocks, the one it stands at lifted off its footprint; the pipeline's lanes and cards
   are slabs, pointing lifts a card up-left off its footprint (G7, G8). */
@layer kp.signature {

/* ── The ideas and the recipe components, in this theme [kpadopt4-ideas, kpadopt4-recipes] ──
   Everything here is a slab or a part of one: a terminal is an ink plate with paper words and a yellow prompt; a time
   left is a disc on its footprint and a digital time a row of blocks, and when the time is out the part is set down
   again, once, on its footprint (G3, G12); a range's pick is the yellow plate; the compare slider's divider is the
   six-pixel bar and its handle a block lifted off its footprint; a wheel turns at a constant speed and stops dead
   (G1: no ease, no settle); an included chip is yellow with a stamped tick, an excluded one is ink with a red cross
   (G5, G16); a step is set down on its footprint (G3). */
@layer kp.signature {

/* ── The new adoption parts in brutalism [t56-brutalism-1018] ──
   A small part is the 2 px line on a 3 px hard shadow (G7): the weekday chips and the small identity mark stand on a
   shadow that never reaches a neighbour, and the shadow of a field keeps a clear gap before the unit that follows it.
   On a phone the labels are set tight, so a day's name, a segment, a Back or Next never breaks mid-word (the 4 px
   margin rule of research/_review/DEMO_RULES.md, chapter 2). */
@layer kp.signature {

